## Board

The layer-matrix **Board** presentation element: a generic kanban over any cards, consuming `KanbanPlane` from boxel-ui (drag engine, columns and WIP limits come free — consume, don't rebuild). The block adds the card-level contract: `@items` (CardDef[]), `@columns` ({key,label,color?}[]), `@columnKeyFor(item)`, and `@onMove(item, columnKey)` fired when a drag crosses columns — the consumer persists the result (e.g. sets `stage` and saves).

```gts
import { Board } from '../board';
<Board
  @items={{this.opps}}
  @columns={{this.stages}}
  @columnKeyFor={{this.stageOf}}
  @onMove={{this.setStage}}
/>
```

Cards render in their own fitted format by default — `KanbanPlane` supplies the sized container, so wrapping cards again produces dead space. Pass a `<:card as |item|>` block to customize. Column `color` tints the column header, which is how a consumer expresses stage semantics without forking the block.

The linked example mounts the board over the pipeline instances, with Opportunity and Deal on one board via adoption.

**Non-goals:** persisting column order or per-card sort order (in-memory only), query-driven item loading (the consumer's job), interactive controls inside cards — the drag engine claims `pointerdown`, so a child that needs its own clicks must stop propagation.
